.TH PRIVACITY 1 "2026-08" "privacity" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
privacity \- VPN Gate auto-connector (daemon-first)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B privacity
[\fB\-c\fR \fIcountry\fR] [\fB\-\-server\fR \fIhost\fR]
[\fB\-\-fast\fR] [\fB\-\-protocol\fR \fItype\fR] [\fIcommand\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fetches the fastest public VPN Gate servers, picks the best one, and
connects via OpenVPN or WireGuard in the background.  Credentials for
public servers (VPN Gate vpn/vpn, VPNBook) are injected automatically,
so no interactive prompt is needed.  Daemon mode is the default.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-country\fR \fIcountry\fR
Filter servers by country name or code (e.g. "Japan", "US", "Korea").
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fIhost\fR
Connect to a specific server from the cached list, by hostname or
country (case-insensitive substring).  Combined with \fB\-c\fR to
narrow the match.  See "privacity list" to find servers.
.TP
\fB\-\-fast\fR
Sort servers by lowest ping (ms) instead of highest score.
.TP
\fB\-\-protocol\fR \fItype\fR
Force VPN protocol: ovpn, wg, or auto (default).
.TP
\fB\-\-log-file\fR \fIpath\fR
Write all output to the given log file (tee).
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show timestamps and detailed output.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B privacity
Daemon mode (default).  Connect to the best server in background.
.TP
.B daemon
Connect in background.  No terminal needed after connection.
.TP
.B daemon \-\-persist
Install systemd user service so the VPN auto-connects after login.
.TP
.B daemon \-\-unpersist
Remove the systemd user service.
.TP
.B list
Show top 20 servers with score and ping, plus available countries.
.TP
.B countries
List all available countries.
.TP
.B disconnect
Tear down the current VPN connection.
.TP
.B reconnect
Pick the best server (optionally filtered by \fB\-c\fR/\fB\-\-server\fR)
and reconnect.
.TP
.B status
Show current connection: server, country, external IP, ping, speed.
.TP
.B speedtest
Measure download and upload speed via Cloudflare and print result in Mbps.
.TP
.B update
Pull the latest version from git and reinstall.
.TP
.B help
Show the help message with all commands and options.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/privacity/config\fR
Configuration file.  Format: \fBKEY=VALUE\fR.
Supported keys: \fBcountry\fR, \fBmode\fR, \fBfast\fR, \fBprotocol\fR.
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/privacity/servers.csv\fR
Cached VPN Gate server list (5 minute TTL).
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/privacity/auth.txt\fR
Credentials for the active public VPN (mode 0600).
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/privacity/active.ovpn\fR
Sanitized OpenVPN config of the active connection.
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/privacity/privacity.pid\fR
PID of the background OpenVPN process.
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/privacity/last_host\fR
Last connected server hostname and country.
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/privacity/openvpn.log\fR
OpenVPN daemon log.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Connect to the best server (daemon)
.B privacity
.TP
Connect to a Japanese server in background
.B privacity \-c Japan
.TP
Connect to the fastest-ping US server
.B privacity \-c US \-\-fast
.TP
Connect to a specific server
.B privacity \-\-server vpn123
.TP
List Korean servers
.B privacity \-c Korea list
.TP
Check current connection
.B privacity status
.TP
Reconnect to a US server
.B privacity \-c US reconnect
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Runtime: openvpn, wget, curl, wg-quick, sudo.
